        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a92d180c-8e7e-51fc-8ee1-2a27f04da7fa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dynasties: Nerva–Antonine dynasty\n- People: Nerva, Trajan, Hadrian, Antoninus Pius, Lucius Verus, Marcus Aurelius, Commodus\n- Roles: Roman Emperors, co-emperor of Rome\n- Artworks: Great Antonine Altar\n\nFacts:\n- The Nerva–Antonine dynasty was a dynasty of seven Roman Emperors who ruled the Roman Empire from 96 AD to 192 AD.\n- The emperors of the Nerva–Antonine dynasty were Nerva, Trajan, Hadrian, Antoninus Pius, Lucius Verus, Marcus Aurelius, and Commodus.\n- Lucius Verus was born on 15 December 130.\n- Lucius Verus was co-emperor of Rome with his adoptive brother Marcus Aurelius from 161 until his death in 169.\n- Lucius Verus died in 169.\n- On the Great Antonine Altar, Lucius Verus stands to the right of Antoninus Pius.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
